00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:33,440
Unfortunately for you, this world
isn't big enough for two giant dragons.

271
00:21:43,180 --> 00:21:45,480
He's about to breathe fire, okay?

272
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:47,437
Now you'll breathe something, too.

273
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:49,177
What do you mean, breathe something?

274
00:21:49,260 --> 00:21:50,090
Let us try!

275
00:21:50,340 --> 00:21:51,440
Do it like Kaido!

276
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:58,459
You act like it's normal
for people to breathe fire!

277
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:00,320
Yes, please!

278
00:22:21,620 --> 00:22:22,560
No, stop!

279
00:22:22,820 --> 00:22:24,160
I'm not here to fight!

280
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:25,360
I'm peaceful!

281
00:22:25,940 --> 00:22:26,860
Hey, Momo!

282
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:29,000
I need you to bite Kaido!

283
00:22:29,260 --> 00:22:30,240
Bite him!

284
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:35,900
Now, third gear!

285
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:39,420
Wait, Luffy!

286
00:22:39,620 --> 00:22:40,620
I can't do that!

287
00:22:40,740 --> 00:22:42,180
You're asking too much!

288
00:22:53,660 --> 00:22:56,000
Time to show him what we can do!

289
00:22:57,780 --> 00:23:00,400
Gum-tum elephant guy!

290
00:23:09,260 --> 00:23:10,090
Hey, Momo!

291
00:23:10,580 --> 00:23:12,540
I need you to bite Kaido!

292
00:23:13,160 --> 00:23:14,380
I can't!

293
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:30,017
Don't worry, I'll make
certain both of you escape.

294
00:23:30,100 --> 00:23:30,930
Just hold on.

295
00:23:31,013 --> 00:23:32,160
I know what to do.

296
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:57,120
Mother, no!

297
00:23:57,860 --> 00:23:58,690
What?

298
00:24:09,180 --> 00:24:11,180
No, no, no, no!

299
00:24:30,320 --> 00:24:32,920
Your father was a fool of a lord.

300
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:36,105
Now tell me your name, dammit!

301
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:37,880
Spineless brat!

302
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:50,840
I'm hurt!

303
00:24:52,760 --> 00:24:54,560
I don't!

304
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:05,220
What the hell are you doing?

305
00:25:05,540 --> 00:25:06,820
Stay out of this!

306
00:25:16,040 --> 00:25:19,800
You'll pay for what you did to
the land of Wano and its people!

307
00:25:20,740 --> 00:25:25,760
If it weren't for you,
father would be here.

308
00:25:26,680 --> 00:25:28,220
Mother would be here!

309
00:25:32,060 --> 00:25:36,060
I said stay out of this,
you pathetic little brat!

310
00:25:43,240 --> 00:25:45,100
Momonosuke, get out of there!

311
00:25:45,700 --> 00:25:46,620
Blast me!

312
00:25:59,100 --> 00:26:00,720
You did it, Momo!

313
00:26:01,440 --> 00:26:02,270
Wait, what?

314
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:03,877
Did he just call him Momo?

315
00:26:03,960 --> 00:26:06,137
That pink dragon is Lord Momonosuke?

316
00:26:06,220 --> 00:26:07,740
Hey, how's that possible?

317
00:26:08,100 --> 00:26:10,240
Our Shogun is doing Wano proud!

318
00:26:30,060 --> 00:26:32,860
Now you know you have
the power to hurt Kaido!

319
00:26:42,820 --> 00:26:48,700
Dragons bring thunderclouds, and
now there are two dragons here.

320
00:26:50,220 --> 00:26:55,140
Your precious moon is gone,
and not a moment too soon.

321
00:26:57,280 --> 00:27:03,257
If I had taken even one more attack, I
would be kneeling in defeat right now.

322
00:27:03,340 --> 00:27:09,040
But the power your Su-Long transformation
grants you is a double-edged sword.

323
00:27:09,280 --> 00:27:11,927
It's left you with no
more strength to fight.

324
00:27:36,080 --> 00:27:38,100
Oh no, his power went away!

325
00:27:38,380 --> 00:27:40,498
We shall come to your reign at once!

326
00:27:42,180 --> 00:27:43,900
You have to wait your time!

327
00:27:49,600 --> 00:27:51,820
The moon didn't betray you.

328
00:27:52,740 --> 00:27:55,460
I just got lickety lucky, that's all.

329
00:27:56,960 --> 00:28:02,040
You had a good run, but now it's
lickety lights out for you, boss cat.

330
00:28:08,440 --> 00:28:09,270
Master!

331
00:28:09,800 --> 00:28:10,630
Master!

332
00:28:14,980 --> 00:28:16,380
Hey, Momo!

333
00:28:18,340 --> 00:28:20,752
You know who you just took a bite out of?

334
00:28:21,620 --> 00:28:23,700
An emperor of the sea!

335
00:28:25,380 --> 00:28:29,200
Is there anything left in the
world that can scare you now?

336
00:28:30,620 --> 00:28:31,450
No.

337
00:28:39,540 --> 00:28:41,340
There isn't!

338
00:28:54,860 --> 00:28:56,237
So fly!

339
00:28:56,320 --> 00:28:58,720
With your eyes open this time!

340
00:28:59,120 --> 00:29:00,180
I shall!

341
00:29:03,340 --> 00:29:04,537
Your job...

342
00:29:04,620 --> 00:29:07,420
is to stop Onigashima!

343
00:29:13,840 --> 00:29:16,420
As for Kaido, I got this!

344
00:29:19,340 --> 00:29:20,240
Hear that?

345
00:29:21,340 --> 00:29:22,780
You're done for!

346
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:47,100
Wolfie's back!

347
00:29:47,660 --> 00:29:50,120
Give him the old war, my boy!

348
00:29:55,840 --> 00:29:59,457
Now this is gonna be...

349
00:29:59,540 --> 00:30:00,380
Super!

350
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:09,460
You're a real riot, Straw Hat.

351
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:14,640
He sure likes to talk, Vic.

352
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:16,939
What's he been doing all this time?

353
00:30:18,720 --> 00:30:19,550
Loopy!

354
00:30:20,440 --> 00:30:21,860
And Momo, too!

355
00:30:22,260 --> 00:30:23,319
Should have known.

356
00:30:23,540 --> 00:30:25,480
He always keeps his word.

357
00:30:25,680 --> 00:30:27,151
That's our Loopy for you.

358
00:30:27,720 --> 00:30:29,080
Go, Vic Root!

359
00:30:31,840 --> 00:30:33,017
You guys.

360
00:30:33,100 --> 00:30:34,880
See you soon, Luffy.

361
00:30:39,960 --> 00:30:42,120
Looks like it's finally time.

362
00:30:43,240 --> 00:30:44,070
Yeah.

363
00:30:44,153 --> 00:30:44,983
Let's get started.

364
00:31:12,880 --> 00:31:18,520
Do you think you have even a
single chance of defeating me?

365
00:31:24,140 --> 00:31:29,760
As long as I'm still alive,
I have infinite chances.

366
00:31:31,580 --> 00:31:32,980
Aaaaaah!

367
00:31:38,120 --> 00:31:39,520
Aaaaaah!

368
00:32:02,320 --> 00:32:07,480
Just like in the journal, Odin wrote about
this when Roger and Whitebeard clashed.

369
00:32:14,780 --> 00:32:17,980
He said the heavens split open.

370
00:32:23,740 --> 00:32:26,940
I have something to report.

371
00:32:28,620 --> 00:32:32,480
The clouds have split.

372
00:32:42,620 --> 00:32:44,740
I've heard enough from you, Karoo.

373
00:32:51,560 --> 00:32:52,390
Ha!

374
00:32:52,500 --> 00:32:53,677
Would you look at that?

375
00:32:53,760 --> 00:32:56,100
Luck sees me back on my side.

376
00:33:10,540 --> 00:33:15,200
I bet you're having a ball
up there, aren't you, Kaido?

377
00:33:17,820 --> 00:33:19,340
Well, boys...

378
00:33:23,180 --> 00:33:26,600
We can't let our friends
show us up, right?

379
00:33:35,300 --> 00:33:38,080
Odin, one sword style!

380
00:33:53,080 --> 00:33:54,640
Divine Frenzy!

381
00:34:02,920 --> 00:34:03,750
Ah!

382
00:34:05,600 --> 00:34:07,040
I'm taking that!

383
00:34:13,600 --> 00:34:17,940
I won't tear you apart, you burglow!

384
00:34:19,420 --> 00:34:23,080
K-9 Cleaver!

385
00:35:04,580 --> 00:35:08,357
Pedro, I wish I could share I'll
share one last drink with you, Karoo,

386
00:35:08,440 --> 00:35:09,969
under this beautiful moon.

387
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:13,791
That was amazing, Master!

388
00:35:14,420 --> 00:35:15,680
Oh, Carrot!

389
00:35:17,320 --> 00:35:18,379
You two are great!

390
00:35:18,500 --> 00:35:19,940
I'm so glad you're okay!

391
00:35:20,820 --> 00:35:23,020
That was a fine performance, Master!

392
00:35:23,740 --> 00:35:24,570
Thanks!

393
00:35:25,340 --> 00:35:27,720
You Karoo did what none of us could!

394
00:35:28,060 --> 00:35:29,277
Pedro is a thing!

395
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:30,380
I would be proud!

396
00:35:32,920 --> 00:35:33,980
Careful, everyone!

397
00:35:37,380 --> 00:35:38,937
The moon's still out.

398
00:35:39,020 --> 00:35:40,961
Yugara don't want to turn Sulong.

399
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:45,077
I wonder what made the clouds clear.

400
00:35:45,160 --> 00:35:48,160
Having some crazy weather
tonight, that's for sure.

401
00:36:05,020 --> 00:36:08,440
Now you know the rage of the meek people.

402
00:36:17,880 --> 00:36:18,821
How can this be?

403
00:36:19,060 --> 00:36:20,320
They took down Jack!

404
00:36:20,980 --> 00:36:25,745
If they can stand up to a lead performer,
who knows what else they're capable of?

405
00:36:28,680 --> 00:36:29,510
No matter.

406
00:36:29,980 --> 00:36:32,920
After all, it's none of my concern now.
